right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How much later? I had to wait a few hours. Which is kind of odd, since that doesn't seem like it would rule out spam or the like after someone figures out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>About 20 minutes<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T06:14:24-07:00","id":1513639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/trouble-tickets/1501447-edit-spam-excess?p=1513610#post1513610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About 20 minutes</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were guessing, I'd assume at least 30 minutes to an hour, minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T04:01:34-07:00","id":1515452,"title":"","content":"I've started a new topic in the Wraith sub-forum - no edits, no links, no bad words - and it got instantly flagged as spam.<br /> <br /> Either I have inadvertently tripped some word filter, or the adaptive thingy is getting worse, not better.<br /> <br /> I think it is possible to set a post threshold (minimum number of posts) to exclude long time users from the filter in BB 5, would that be an option?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T20:11:47-07:00","id":1516309,"title":"","content":"Uh, hey. Some of my posts in the law and ethics thread seem to be stuck in unapproved purgatory. Is there any chance someone can reapprove them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:18:10-07:00","id":1516534,"title":"","content":"How long do we have to wait on edits, because I have a post in the Mage forum I waited almost 40 minutes to edit and it still got flagged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:16:25-07:00","id":1516570,"title":"","content":"While time seems to have some level of impact on the bot's algorithm it's a black box variable, not something reliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T21:53:10-07:00","id":1516608,"title":"","content":"I have a habit of not thoroughly checking my stuff, and finding grammatical mistakes immediately after posting. I can usually get away with immediately editing a post, with maybe a minute delay. Afterwords? I get flagged every time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T00:36:23-07:00","id":1516618,"title":"","content":"Not to diminish how annoying this is (Arc and Temple have posts in limbo in the same thread that's kinda stalled because of it), but it's worth remembering that machine learning is really counter-intuitive to human learning.<br /> <br /> Even fairly rudimentary machine learning tends to occasionally do what seems like flying off the rails instead of refining its inputs more incrementally. Think about it like when a very good Wordle player looking at two greens and two yellows abandons all four known letters for a word using five completely unused letters. Logically this is optimal behavior. It's a fast way to receive feedback on a bunch of unknown variables that can then expedite solving the puzzle by drastically narrowing the possibilities. But the instinctive response most humans have because of how we learn is to stick with the letters we already know and try to get them lined up properly; which can easily mean running out of guesses.<br /> <br /> You see this a lot in robotics and AI testing. It feels like the system is getting really close to what you're trying to train it to do, but then it goes off the walls. To us, it's exceedingly frustrating because we can see how close it was, and don't have the response of, &quot;lets do something completely different to double check a bunch of variables at once,&quot; as an average learning instinct. To the bot, flagging a good post as bad and get corrected by the mods, can be weighed as more valuable data because it confirms the model's accuracy. It can't even start to think about our frustration as being a false-negative test for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T19:16:21-07:00","id":1519146,"title":"","content":"Sigh. Worst thing about a WIR is that you check the text and realise you misspelled a word and had wrong separations between your paragraphs. You edit, and you doom it to unapproved hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T08:10:27-07:00","id":1519170,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've been having some issues with that, as well. It seems to be a tad bit unpredictable, since sometimes I might edit it, realize I missed something, then go back and edit it, realized I missed something <i>else</i>, and then that trips spam detection. One other time it's been on the first go. I'm trying to stay off the edit button for the time being but my typing is far from perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Project to convert Chronicles of Darkness to a data-driven <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499154-homebrew-vehicular-and-combined-arms-combat-in-cofd\" target=\"_blank\">Combined Arms Simulation: Gods of Iron</a><br /> My personal website, projects and games: <a href=\"https://puckerfactorgames.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://puckerfactorgames.com</a>","edited":{"userid":27707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27707-jester-pfg","user":"Jester-PFG","date":".  Missed something... 07-30-2023, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27707-jester-pfg","name":"Jeste